# Milestone 03A — Mathematically Correct WSST Reconstruction

Agent implementation specification · SynchroSqueezing.jl · Corrective milestone before ridge extraction

## Objective

Establish a mathematically consistent implementation of the first-order wavelet synchrosqueezed transform (WSST) and its inverse, independent of the particular Julia wavelet library used to compute the CWT.

The package must support two essential operations:

1. Full oscillatory reconstruction: recover the signal's represented oscillatory content from all synchrosqueezed coefficients.
2. Individual component reconstruction: recover a physical oscillatory component by integrating only coefficients within a time-dependent frequency band.

The second operation is particularly important for your future BNS post-merger analysis.

The existing Milestone 03 implementation should be audited and reused wherever mathematically correct. We should not rewrite working thresholding, grid generation, phase estimation, deposition, or test infrastructure simply because the inverse needs reconsideration.

## 1. Scientific decision

Adopt the standard analytic-CWT-based synchrosqueezing formulation used by `ssqueezepy` as the reference mathematical convention.

The source of `ssqueezepy` confirms that `issq_cwt` reconstructs a real signal by summing selected complex SST coefficients, taking their real part, and applying the wavelet admissibility coefficient. Its component reconstruction uses the same operation restricted to selected time-frequency bins.&#x20;

